From ba32058771edebe18f01505c29fb0bc85811a631 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:18:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Assign feeds to many download rules at once

Selecting rules now offers a feed button that opens a dialog with one
tri-state checkbox per feed (all / none / some of the selected rules use
it). Ticking adds the feed to every selected rule, unticking removes it,
mixed boxes are left alone. Disabled rules that get a feed (e.g. imported
from qBittorrent without a subscribed feed) can be turned on in the same
step, and applying to existing articles is opt-in.

- POST /api/rss/rules/feeds updates all rules in one request
- Rules list can be filtered by feed, or by "no feed" (applies to all)
- Warns when rules that used every feed get limited, or end up with none

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013nmSf2zmYoNEfzcNutPGUX
